---
alwaysApply: false
description : How To invoke a Supabase edge function
---
Always follow this pattern to create an edge function.

Key points:

- Let's try to pass as few parameters as possible in edge function. Ideally, update the related table in supbabase first and then call the edge function with worksapceId and itemId (documentId, ...). Edge function will retrieve information from db directly, or even pass this id to the data API and the data API will fetch the information itself.
- Check that the user is authenticated. Ensure that when a row is read or updated, the `workspace_id` belongs to the list of workspaces the user belongs to (especially if `workspace_id` is part of the request body).
- Dual-mode auth for all new Edge Functions:
  - Client mode (JWT): derive `user_id` from the JWT via `supabase.auth.getUser(token)` and override any incoming `user_id` in the payload (prevent spoofing).
  - Server/Cron mode (service role): if `Authorization` exactly matches `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`, read `user_id` from the request body (or `ef_body.user_id`) and require it; then validate membership against `users_workspaces_map`.
  - Always validate `(user_id, workspace_id)` in `users_workspaces_map` before performing operations.
  - If the goal is to display errors in the frontend, return HTTP 200 with `{ error, status_code }` per rule below.
- When returning an error, use the appropriate HTTP status code EXCEPT when the goal is to display the error content on the front end. If the status is not 200, the front end may not be able to read the content. In that case, use 200 as the status code but include a JSON payload such as:

{error: "my message", status_code: 402} // To display the message content on the front end

- When dealing with document, check if document is ".doc" and if yes, call the shared function :

import convertDocToDocx from "../_shared/doc-to-docx-converter.ts";

and convert to doc to docx, with potentially replace the relateed path and name of file by the docx version, if needed.

 if (/\.doc$/i.test(docData.file_path)) {
     
     
      try {
        // Shared helper performs DOC→DOCX via external service and uploads to the same bucket.
        const { outputFilePath } = await convertDocToDocx(
          supabase,
          <bucket-name>,
          docData.file_path
        );
        // Persist the new path in DB; we do not request returning rows for performance.
        const { error: updateErr } = await supabase
          .from(<table_name>)
          .update({ file_path: outputFilePath, name : (/\.doc$/i.test(docData.name)) ? docData.name.replace('.doc', '.docx') : docData.name })
          .eq('id', documentId);
        if (!updateErr) {
          docData.file_path = outputFilePath;
        } 
      } catch (err) {
        console.error(
          ` DOC→DOCX conversion failed for ${docData.file_path}`,
          err
        );
      }
    }

- When updating Supabase DB or Storage, you can use elevated privileges by assuming the Postgres role using the correct Supabase Edge Function secret. See below.
- When done, always show the CLI to deploy the edge function to dev to the user. Keep this projet ref as is, only want to copy past it.

e.g : npx supabase functions deploy my-function-name --project-ref htbkflogiaxswzpxtsoz.

Show it in a bash section so that user can just click on "run" if he wants. Never run it on his behalf.


Example:

(This example calls an external DATA API; this part can be changed if needed (e.g., call another external API, n8n, update Supabase, ...))

import { serve } from "https://deno.land/std@0.168.0/http/server.ts";
import { createClient } from "https://esm.sh/@supabase/supabase-js@2.7.1";

// CORS handling to avoid cross-origin errors in the front end
const corsHeaders = {
  "Access-Control-Allow-Origin": "*",
  "Access-Control-Allow-Headers": "authorization, x-client-info, apikey, content-type",
};

const CHECK_FOR_CREDITS = false;
serve(async (req) => {
  // Handle OPTIONS (CORS preflight) requests
  if (req.method === "OPTIONS") {
    return new Response(null, { headers: corsHeaders });
  }

  try {
    if (req.method !== "POST") {
      return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: "Method not allowed" }), {
        headers: { ...corsHeaders, "Content-Type": "application/json" },
        status: 405,
      });
    }

    // Initialize Supabase client with the service role key
    const supabase = createClient(
      Deno.env.get("SUPABASE_URL") ?? "",
      Deno.env.get("SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY") ?? ""
    );

    // Dual-mode auth: client (JWT) vs server (service role)
    const authHeader = req.headers.get("Authorization");
    if (!authHeader) {
      return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: "User not authenticated" }), {
        headers: { ...corsHeaders, "Content-Type": "application/json" },
        status: 401,
      });
    }
    const token = authHeader.replace("Bearer ", "").trim();
    const serviceKey = (Deno.env.get("SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY") ?? "").trim();
    let userId: string | null = null;
    if (token === serviceKey) {
      userId = body.userId ?? body?.user_id ;
      if (!userId) {
        return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: "user_id required in body for server mode" }), {
          headers: { ...corsHeaders, "Content-Type": "application/json" },
          status: 400,
        });
      }
    } else {
      const { data: user, error: userError } = await supabase.auth.getUser(token);
      userId = user?.user?.id ?? null;
      if (userError || !userId) {
        return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: "Unable to retrieve user" }), {
          headers: { ...corsHeaders, "Content-Type": "application/json" },
          status: 401,
        });
      }
     
    }
    const body = await req.json();

    if (userError || !userId) {
      return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: "Unable to retrieve user" }), {
        headers: { ...corsHeaders, "Content-Type": "application/json" },
        status: 401,
      });
    }

    const { data: workspace, error: useError2 } = await supabase
      .from("users_workspaces_map")
      .select("*")
      .eq("user_id", userId)
      .eq("workspace_id", body.workspaceId)
      .single();

    if (useError2 || !workspace?.workspace_id) {
      return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: "The user does not belong to the workspace" }), {
        headers: { ...corsHeaders, "Content-Type": "application/json" },
        status: 401,
      });
    }

    if (CHECK_FOR_CREDITS) {
      const nbCredits = 1; // Credits to add

      const { data: hasEnoughCredits, error: errorCredits } = await supabase
        .rpc("increment_total_usage_credits", { workspace_uuid: body.workspaceId, nb_credits: nbCredits });

      console.log(`Increment credits of ${nbCredits} returned hasEnough`, hasEnoughCredits);

      if (errorCredits) {
        return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: "Error incrementing credits" }), {
          headers: { ...corsHeaders, "Content-Type": "application/json" },
          status: 402,
        });
      }

      if (!hasEnoughCredits) {
        return new Response(
          JSON.stringify({ error: "Not enough credits", status_code: 402 }), // cannot retrieve status code via actual error
          { headers: { ...corsHeaders, "Content-Type": "application/json" }, status: 200 }
        );
      }
    }

    // Environment variables
    const API_KEY = Deno.env.get("DATA_API_KEY");
    const ROOT_URL = Deno.env.get("ROOT_URL") || "https://ai-assistant-prod-jybetmkkea-ew.a.run.app";

    const API_URL = `${ROOT_URL}/url_example/`;

    if (!API_KEY || !API_URL) {
      return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: "Missing API configuration" }), {
        headers: { ...corsHeaders, "Content-Type": "application/json" },
        status: 500,
      });
    }
    // Generate the final request body

    const final_body = {
      client_id: workspace?.workspace_id,
      user_id: userId,
      bubble_env: Deno.env.get("ENV_SUPA"),
    };

    // Example usage: Call the external API with the user ID
    const response = await fetch(API_URL, {
      method: "POST",
      headers: {
        "Content-Type": "application/json",
        Authorization: `${API_KEY}`,
      },
      body: JSON.stringify(final_body),
    });

    if (!response.ok) {
      return new Response(
        JSON.stringify({ error: "External API failed", details: await response.text() }),
        { headers: { ...corsHeaders, "Content-Type": "application/json" }, status: response.status }
      );
    }

    const result = await response.json();
    if (!result["success"]) {
      return new Response(
        JSON.stringify({ error: "External API failed", details: await response.text() }),
        { headers: { ...corsHeaders, "Content-Type": "application/json" }, status: response.status }
      );
    }

    const final_result = {
      result,
    };

    const { error: insertResultLogs } = await supabase.from(<example_log_data>).insert([final_result]);

    // Return the response to the front end
    return new Response(JSON.stringify(final_result), {
      headers: { ...corsHeaders, "Content-Type": "application/json" },
      status: 200,
    });

  } catch (err) {
    return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: "Internal error", details: err.message }), {
      headers: { ...corsHeaders, "Content-Type": "application/json" },
      status: 500,
    });
  }
});